; BOUNCE BONANZA - song 8, course 1 "First Roll": "First Roll" (SPEC.md 137.20)
;
; F major at 136.5 BPM with a breath of swing: a 16th is a row, and the rows
; alternate seven and five sub-ticks (`groove 7 5`), so an 8th is always 12
; and only the off-beat 16ths land a little late - the skip of a rubber ball
; that has just been set rolling. A pattern is two bars of 4/4, 3.5 s.
;
; The player's FIRST course, so the tune is welcoming and sure of itself,
; never tense: plain I - IV - V harmony with one turn round the subdominant
; side, F Bb | F C | F Bb | Gm7 C7 F, and a bridge that visits the relative
; minor without dwelling there, Bb C | Am Dm | Gm C | Bb C7.
;
; The intro is the ball being tapped onto the course over C - C7: three taps
; on G (a note, a 16th rest, a late 16th, a note) while the bass and the beat
; set off alone, then a roll up the C7 arpeggio and back down onto the tune.
; A's MOTIF is a HOP AND A ROLL - a chord tone, a skip down a third on the
; swung 16th, back up and over to the fifth, a rest, then two quick notes
; rolling down onto the third:
;   a8 r16 f16 a8 >c8 r8 <a8 >c16 <b-16 a8      (over F)
; answered a step higher on Bb; the second statement runs up to F5 and down
; to a half close on C7, with a two-16th pickup back in; the fourth phrase
; squeezes the hop onto Gm7 - C7 and lands on F with the chiparp's sparkle.
; B turns to the GLOCKENSPIEL over a plucked harp pushing 3 + 3 + 2 and a
; held bass: short arpeggio bounces climbing (Bb, C, Am), a step-wise
; settle on Dm, then a scale that the horn takes over and runs down through
; C7 onto the motif. Intro, A A' B A'' for ever: the loop is 10 patterns,
; 35.2 s, about one first run of the course.
;
; Style borrowed, not notes: Fairway's two-bar patterns, its swung-16th
; pickups and its bridge handed to the glockenspiel; Bounce Trial's
; off-beat stabs and octave-popping pluck bass; Summit Rush's 3 + 3 + 2 push
; (here on the harp, in the bridge).
;
; THE SPEAKER: the lead carries it. Kick and snare blip on the beats (the
; hats and the claps' rasp are the AdLib's), and `spkbass` fills the lead's
; rests with the bass: the intro's taps, and the 8th rest in the middle of
; every motif becomes a low bounce under the ball. Every phrase names its
; own instrument and volume at its start and a lead phrase that leaves the
; horn comes back to it, so no phrase inherits a state its packing did not
; assume. `spkring`: the chiparp's arpeggios RING on the speaker, a drum keyed
; inside one the chip's alone; the horn's scoop does not loop, so it is no
; arpeggio and the beat still blips under the horn.

song firstroll "First Roll"
groove 7 5
unit 16
rows 32
measure 16
spkbass
spkring
voice lead horn
voice bass pluckbass
voice chord stab

; --- the intro: the ball tapped onto the course, C | C7 ------------------------
; (revised after the owner's first listen: the speaker's intro read better than
; the AdLib's.) The speaker plays only the lead and, in its rests, the bass, so
; the taps on G4 stood alone; the AdLib laid an off-beat C stab - holding G4
; itself - under every beat of bar 1, and a C7 stab in the roll's own octave
; under bar 2, so the taps and the roll were buried in their own register, and
; the horn's soft attack hardly spoke on a short tap. Now the TAPS are the
; glockenspiel (a struck, percussive note: a ball tapped), bar 1 has no chord
; at all - the taps, the bass and the beat - and bar 2's C7 is one soft harp
; chord BELOW the roll, with a single stab pushing into A. The speaker hears
; the same pitches at the same times (it plays neither chord nor volume),
; less the horn's one-sub-tick scoop on the three taps.
lead LI = @glock v14 r2 o4 g8 r16 g16 g8 r8 | @horn v13 c8 e8 g8 b-8 >c8 <b-8 g16 e16 g8 |
bass BI = o2 c4 >c8 <c8 g4 r8 g8 | c4 >c8 <c8 g4 b-8 >c8 |
chord CI = @harp v8 o3 r1 | [g b- >e]2 r4 r8 @stab q6 [g b- >e]8 |
drum DI = k4 h8 h8 s4 h8 h8 | k4 h8 h8 s8 s16 s16 T8 t8 |

; The stabs land on every off-beat 8th: a note a quarter long gated (q18) to
; half an 8th, so a bar of four stabs is four events and no rests; a stab
; holds its chord across the bar line, which is why these carry no `|`.

; --- A: the hop and the roll ------------------------------------------------------
lead LA1 = @horn v13 o4 a8 r16 f16 a8 >c8 r8 <a8 >c16 <b-16 a8 |
           b-8 r16 g16 b-8 >d8 r8 c8 <b-8 g8 |
lead LA2 = @horn v13 o4 a8 r16 f16 a8 >c8 f8 e8 d8 c8 |
           <b-8 >c8 d8 <b-8 g4 r8 e16 g16 |
lead LA3 = @horn v13 o4 b-8 r16 g16 b-8 >d8 c8 r16 <g16 b-8 >e8 |
           f8 c8 <a8 >c8 @chiparp f4 @horn r8 o4 e16 g16 |
bass BA1 = o2 f4 >f8 <f8 c4 r8 a8 | b-4 >b-8 <b-8 f4 r8 a8 |
bass BA2 = o2 f4 >f8 <f8 c4 r8 a8 | c4 >c8 <c8 g4 r8 e8 |
bass BA3 = o2 g4 >g8 <g8 c4 >c8 <c8 | f4 >f8 <f8 c4 r8 a8 |
chord CA1 = @stab v10 o4 r8 q18 [f a >c]4 [f a >c]4 [f a >c]4 [f a >c]4 [f b- >d]4 [f b- >d]4 [f b- >d]4 q6 [f b- >d]8
chord CA2 = @stab v10 o4 r8 q18 [f a >c]4 [f a >c]4 [f a >c]4 [f a >c]4 [e g >c]4 [e g >c]4 [e g b-]4 q6 [e g b-]8
chord CA3 = @stab v10 o4 r8 q18 [f b- >d]4 [f b- >d]4 [e g b-]4 [e g b-]4 [f a >c]4 [f a >c]4 [f a >c]4 q6 [f a >c]8
drum DA = k8 h8 s8 h8 k8 h8 s8 h8 | k8 h8 s8 h16 k16 k8 h8 s8 h8 |
drum DF = k8 h8 s8 h8 k8 h8 s8 h8 | k8 h8 s8 h8 k8 s16 s16 T16 T16 t8 |

; --- B: the bridge, on the glockenspiel over the harp's push ----------------------
lead LB1 = @glock v13 o5 f8 d8 r16 <b-16 >d8 c4 <b-4 | >e8 c8 r16 <g16 >c8 e4 g4 |
lead LB2 = @glock v13 o5 e8 c8 r16 <a16 >c8 e4 a4 | f8 e8 d8 c8 d4. r8 |
lead LB3 = @glock v13 o5 d8 <b-8 r16 g16 b-8 >d4 g4 | e8 f8 g8 e8 c4 r8 g16 a16 |
lead LB4 = @glock v13 o5 b-8 a8 g8 f8 d4 f8 b-8 | @horn v13 a8 g8 f8 e8 d8 c8 <b-8 g8 |
bass BB1 = o2 b-2 f4. a8 | >c2 <g4. b8 |
bass BB2 = o2 a2 e4. g8 | d2 a4. f8 |
bass BB3 = o2 g2 d4. f8 | c2 g4. a8 |
bass BB4 = o2 b-2 f4. a8 | >c4 <g4 >c8 <b-8 g8 e8 |
chord CB1 = @harp v10 o4 [f b- >d]4. [f b- >d]4. [f b- >d]4 | [e g >c]4. [e g >c]4. [e g >c]4 |
chord CB2 = @harp v10 o4 [e a >c]4. [e a >c]4. [e a >c]4 | [f a >d]4. [f a >d]4. [f a >d]4 |
chord CB3 = @harp v10 o4 [g b- >d]4. [g b- >d]4. [g b- >d]4 | [e g >c]4. [e g >c]4. [e g >c]4 |
chord CB4 = @harp v10 o4 [f b- >d]4. [f b- >d]4. [f b- >d]4 | [e g b-]4. [e g b-]4. [e g b-]4 |
drum DB = k4 h8 h16 h16 c4 h8 k8 | k4 h8 h16 h16 c4 h8 h8 |

order LI  BI  CI  DI          ; 0: the intro, C C7
order LA1 BA1 CA1 DA          ; 1: A   F Bb - the loop comes back here
order LA2 BA2 CA2 DF          ; 2:     F C(7), the half close
order LA1 BA1 CA1 DA          ; 3: A'  F Bb
order LA3 BA3 CA3 DF          ; 4:     Gm7 C7 F, the full close
order LB1 BB1 CB1 DB          ; 5: B   Bb C
order LB2 BB2 CB2 DB          ; 6:     Am Dm
order LB3 BB3 CB3 DB          ; 7:     Gm C
order LB4 BB4 CB4 DF          ; 8:     Bb C7, the run home
order LA1 BA1 CA1 DA          ; 9: A'' F Bb
order LA3 BA3 CA3 DF          ; 10:    Gm7 C7 F
loop 1
